{"id": "ru-82366d379093.en", "jokeId": "ru-82366d379093", "locale": "en", "adaptation": "direct", "notes": "Line-by-line translation; kilo → two pounds, one and a half kilos → three pounds (same ratio). Narration split where the butcher's action changes. New scales set piece at the counter: the butcher stands behind it, walks to the shelf (freezer) and picks up the chicken, walks back and puts it on the pan (it stays there), picks it up again and carries it back, looks it over, puts it on the scales again and presses with his finger (point). The scales request is dropped.", "title": "The Only Chicken", "location": "magazin", "cast": ["devushka", "barmen"], "roles": {"devushka": "customer", "barmen": "salesman"}, "lines": [{"character": "narrator", "text": "A butcher shop, one minute to closing.", "emotion": "neutral", "pauseAfterSec": 0}, {"character": "narrator", "text": "A breathless woman runs in and says:", "emotion": "surprised", "pauseAfterSec": 0}, {"character": "devushka", "text": "Thank God, I made it! Do you have any chickens?", "emotion": "happy", "pauseAfterSec": 0}, {"character": "narrator", "text": "The butcher takes the only chicken out of the freezer", "emotion": "neutral", "pauseAfterSec": 0}, {"character": "narrator", "text": "and puts it on the scales. The scales show two pounds. The woman:", "emotion": "neutral", "pauseAfterSec": 0}, {"character": "devushka", "text": "Hmm... Don't you have a bigger one?", "emotion": "sad", "pauseAfterSec": 0}, {"character": "narrator", "text": "The butcher puts the chicken back,", "emotion": "neutral", "pauseAfterSec": 0}, {"character": "narrator", "text": "then takes the same one out again, turns it over,", "emotion": "neutral", "pauseAfterSec": 0}, {"character": "narrator", "text": "puts it on the scales and presses down on it with his finger.", "emotion": "smug", "pauseAfterSec": 0}, {"character": "narrator", "text": "The scales show three pounds. The woman:", "emotion": "neutral", "pauseAfterSec": 0}, {"chara